    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d741">

                <pb facs="0834" n="640" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg640"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.CC/7–3145: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 741<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Alternate Delegate to the Preparatory
                        Commission of the United Nations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gerig</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Director of the Office of Special Political
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hiss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">and
                        the Deputy Director of the Office of Special Political Affairs</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ross</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d741-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">plain</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-31">July 31, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7709. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Copre</hi> 4. From Gerig for Hiss and Ross.</p>
                <p>Regarding officers for ExCom (Executive Committee) and PreCo (Preparatory
                    Committee) agreement of Soviet awaited on proposal at Potsdam of rotation among
                    five powers in ExCom with small or middle-sized powers as officers of
                    PreCo.…</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d741-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d741-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the Acting Secretary of State over the signature of Winant.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
